{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/971242-solar-charm-experiment","id":971242,"title":"Solar Charm Experiment","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-17T04:07:17-07:00","id":971242,"title":"Solar Charm Experiment","content":"Let's imagine a Charm. It would go something like this...<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Indomitable Captain's Balance</b><br /> <br /> <b>Cost</b>: -; <b>Mins</b>: Sail 4, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords</b>: None<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Safe Bearing Technique<br /> <br /> A captain who conquered the sea at the height of its wrath laughs in contempt at the feeble blows and arrows of mere men. Every time the Solar stunts her Parry or Evasion in a way that recalls her trials at navigating naval hazards or evokes imagery related to shipboard movement, she immediately regains three motes spent on Charms enhancing her defense.<br /> <br /> <br /> Is such an effect reasonable or desirable to have in the game? Balanced for its cost and the difficulty of acquisition? Does it fit into the underlying design structure of the Solar charmset? Make your case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T04:11:33-07:00","id":971244,"title":"","content":"As a Permanent Charm, affecting Evasion or Parry, guaranteeing extra mote regen for what's essentially a one-point stunt (but in no way inhibiting <i>actual</i> one-point stunts and the bonuses granted therein)? <br /> <br /> I don't much care for it, and I think adding it could potentially unbalance the game; on the other hand, Creation would see a lot more Sail-focused Exalts, and that's always a good thing. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Compare the other Solar Charms that alter your mote recovery. This one is far superior to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 09-17-2016, 07:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T04:13:56-07:00","id":971247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/971242-solar-charm-experiment?p=971244#post971244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a Permanent Charm, affecting Evasion or Parry, guaranteeing extra mote regen for what's essentially a one-die stunt?<br /> <br /> I don't much care for it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> On a scale of &quot;meh&quot; to &quot;this is pants-on-fire insane&quot;, exactly how bad is it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T04:16:39-07:00","id":971249,"title":"","content":"Your post Ninja'd my edit. Which is to say, it's a little crazy, but at least the pants are still on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T04:26:17-07:00","id":971250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/971242-solar-charm-experiment?p=971244#post971244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">on the other hand, Creation would see a lot more Sail-focused Exalts, and that's always a good thing. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Compare the other Solar Charms that alter your mote recovery. This one is far superior to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't it bad for a niche build that requires fairly trivial investment to warp the game around itself to the point where even dedicated specialists are strongly incentivized to dip into it, regardless of concept?<br /> <br /> Moreover: doesn't it go against the fundamental design philosophy of Solars to have a vastly superior combat Charm tucked into an ability that has only passing relevance to combat at best?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T05:13:19-07:00","id":971262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/971242-solar-charm-experiment?p=971250#post971250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't it bad for a niche build that requires fairly trivial investment to warp the game around itself to the point where even dedicated specialists are strongly incentivized to dip into it, regardless of concept?<br /> <br /> Moreover: doesn't it go against the fundamental design philosophy of Solars to have a vastly superior combat Charm tucked into an ability that has only passing relevance to combat at best?</div> </div> </div> </div>Both of these things are true; my &quot;on the other hand&quot; was in jest, hence the &quot;<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />&quot; smiley. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong: it's strong - <i>crazy strong, in fact</i> - but it's far from the end-all, be-all of combat builds. With the investments your Sail guy is having to spend, the Melee guy is buying that many more Melee Charms, and may be able to put Sail guy down before the mote regen becomes an issue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 09-17-2016, 08:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T05:42:23-07:00","id":971273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/971242-solar-charm-experiment?p=971262#post971262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't get me wrong: it's strong - <i>crazy strong, in fact</i> - but it's far from the end-all, be-all of combat builds. With the investments your Sail guy is having to spend, the Melee guy is buying that many more Melee Charms, and may be able to put Sail guy down before the mote regen becomes an issue.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Sail guy only needs three Charms and four ability dots, which is basically one freebie. If Sail guy buys a decent defensive suite, he can fairly easily draw the fight out long enough to win on mote regen alone (if he goes for Snake and Dodge, he can basically say &quot;for 1m, you need 11 successes to be able hit my stunted defense (albeit I may need to spend 1-3 extra motes to no-sell 9+ suxx&quot;).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T08:04:30-07:00","id":971322,"title":"","content":"Look, dude, I already said it was crazy strong. I don't know what you're trying to do, here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T12:04:49-07:00","id":971441,"title":"","content":"You know, you'd probably get better answers if you just asked &quot;hey, does Battle Dancer Method seem really strong to anyone else?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11517-bozwevial","name":"Bozwevial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T12:59:37-07:00","id":971479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bozwevial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/971242-solar-charm-experiment?p=971441#post971441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, you'd probably get better answers if you just asked &quot;hey, does Battle Dancer Method seem really strong to anyone else?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>According to the clarifications given, that one is balanced by the need to flurry (or to use during one of the Charms on that tree that are dances, but then you are not attacking as those are simple Charms and thus can't be flurried)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T13:55:47-07:00","id":971507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/971242-solar-charm-experiment?p=971322#post971322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Look, dude, I already said it was crazy strong. I don't know what you're trying to do, here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's imagine there's a poster who wants to say that a charm is overpowered. They do so by creating a thread in which they invent a completely new charm and then ask people questions about it, questions designed to lead to specific answers that will somehow prove their point.<br /> <br /> On a scale from one to ten, how would you rate that poster's ability to communicate clearly and effectively?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T14:03:21-07:00","id":971515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/971242-solar-charm-experiment?p=971507#post971507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Let's imagine there's a poster who wants to say that a charm is overpowered. They do so by creating a thread in which they invent a completely new charm and then ask people questions about it, questions designed to lead to specific answers that will somehow prove their point.<br /> <br /> On a scale from one to ten, how would you rate that poster's ability to communicate clearly and effectively?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd probably say that this hypothetical person doesn't understand what Battle Dancer Method actually does and the downsides that it has.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11456-nihnoz","name":"nihnoz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11456_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T14:17:04-07:00","id":971520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/971242-solar-charm-experiment?p=971479#post971479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> According to the clarifications given, that one is balanced by the need to flurry (or to use during one of the Charms on that tree that are dances, but then you are not attacking as those are simple Charms and thus can't be flurried)</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, which is a clarification that would have been made earlier had the original question referenced the charm in question and not posed the hypothetical. It's understandable, though - if you see the charm as a cheap defense booster you get just by stunting it's very different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11517-bozwevial","user":"Bozwevial","date":". 09-17-2016, 05:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11517-bozwevial","name":"Bozwevial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T14:42:43-07:00","id":971525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/971242-solar-charm-experiment#post971242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's imagine a Charm. It would go something like this...<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Indomitable Captain's Balance</b><br /> <br /> <b>Cost</b>: -; <b>Mins</b>: Sail 4, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords</b>: None<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Safe Bearing Technique<br /> <br /> A captain who conquered the sea at the height of its wrath laughs in contempt at the feeble blows and arrows of mere men. Every time the Solar stunts her Parry or Evasion in a way that recalls her trials at navigating naval hazards or evokes imagery related to shipboard movement, she immediately regains three motes spent on Charms enhancing her defense.<br /> <br /> <br /> Is such an effect reasonable or desirable to have in the game? Balanced for its cost and the difficulty of acquisition? Does it fit into the underlying design structure of the Solar charmset? Make your case.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I would say it needs to be restricted quite sharply. Compare it against, say, Essence-Gathering Temper, and it looks better than this already amazing Charm.<br /> <br /> There are a few possible solutions to reduce its impact but my preferred fix is this: Once per scene, unless reset by a dynamic change in battle conditions that the Solar can stunt to recall his naval background, such as a storm breaking out or the fight continuing as the building collapses under bombardment. <br /> <br /> Even if you don't get to use it twice, a free boost of 3m every combat is worth more than a lot of Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T15:11:40-07:00","id":971532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/971242-solar-charm-experiment?p=971507#post971507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's imagine there's a poster who wants to say that a charm is overpowered. They do so by creating a thread in which they invent a completely new charm and then ask people questions about it, questions designed to lead to specific answers that will somehow prove their point.<br /> <br /> On a scale from one to ten, how would you rate that poster's ability to communicate clearly and effectively?</div> </div> </div> </div>See, my understanding of Battle Dancer Method was so firmly entrenched in the &quot;you have to actually dance&quot; camp that it didn't even occur to me to consider this hypothetical a reference to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T15:39:35-07:00","id":971544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/971242-solar-charm-experiment?p=971532#post971532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See, my understanding of Battle Dancer Method was so firmly entrenched in the &quot;you have to actually dance&quot; camp that it didn't even occur to me to consider this hypothetical a reference to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Same. I've seen the question asked three different ways to the developers and gotten the exact same answer. You gotta flurry the social influence action, it's not about a stunt.<br /> <br /> Stunting won't hurt you though.<br /> <br /> Couldn't you have just asked about Battle Dancer Method directly?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T16:31:47-07:00","id":971567,"title":"","content":"That would have been too easy, apparently.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T03:18:41-07:00","id":971855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/971242-solar-charm-experiment?p=971544#post971544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Couldn't you have just asked about Battle Dancer Method directly?</div> </div> </div> </div>Look, when people are being shown quotes from <i>multiple developers,</i> have the fluff-crunch distinction explained to them repeatedly, and they still insist that the flavor text of the Dreaming Pearl Courtesan style means they should be able to use it with no flurry requirements &quot;because Silver-Voiced Nightingale allows for social influence without flurry penalties too&quot;, the &quot;communicate clearly and efficiently&quot; method apparently is not working.<br /> <br /> Egads, my players frustrate me sometimes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":3443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","user":"aluminiumtrioxid","date":". 09-18-2016, 06:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T03:56:55-07:00","id":971862,"title":"","content":"So, you have a problem with your players, and instead of settling it, you hop on the forums to (backhandedly!) complain not about the players, but the Charm they're misinterpreting?<br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong, I've had players frustrate me too, but you could have been straightforward about it; we wasted nearly a page because you wouldn't just tell us your problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 09-18-2016, 06:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T04:30:15-07:00","id":971876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/971242-solar-charm-experiment?p=971862#post971862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, you have a problem with your players, and instead of settling it, you hop on the forums to (backhandedly!) complain not about the players, but the Charm they're misinterpreting?</div> </div> </div> </div>That strikes me as a fairly unkind reading. It's more like...<br /> <br /> The player is clearly misinterpreting the Charm, and is quite resistant to attempts to correct that misinterpretation, arguing that the only reason I - and, by extension, members of the Exalted community who don't share their interpretation - refuse to accept it is because I hate the aesthetics of a combatant who fights with the grace and elegance of a dancer and want to make it as ineffective as possible. Which is... fine. I get it. We can sometimes get really invested in character concepts and build ideas, and react with hostility to what we perceive as attacks on said concepts and ideas. But their interpretation is, frankly, ridiculously overpowered. A 3m mote drip every time you're attacked isn't just &quot;a top-tier effect&quot;, it essentially decides any fight against opponents who are not overbearingly more powerful than the character, because at the end of the day, the person who still has motes to enhance their decisives <i>after </i>their opponent has ran out wins.<br /> Therefore, to illustrate what exactly the problem is, I brought up a hypothetical example <i>divorced from the aesthetics the player is so incredibly attached to, </i>in the hopes that with no personal stake in the argument, they'll actually be willing to listen. Except, well, only few people brought up reasons - of which there are many, all of them good - why the described effect isn't healthy for the game. So here we are now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":3443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","user":"aluminiumtrioxid","date":". 09-18-2016, 07:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T05:24:39-07:00","id":971891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/971242-solar-charm-experiment?p=971876#post971876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The player is clearly misinterpreting the Charm, and is quite resistant to attempts to correct that misinterpretation, arguing that the only reason I - and, by extension, members of the Exalted community who don't share their interpretation - refuse to accept it is because I hate the aesthetics of a combatant who fights with the grace and elegance of a dancer and want to make it as ineffective as possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, just to be clear, I don't think it's just members of the Exalted community, John M\u00f8rke (who wrote the Charm) <a href=\"https://twitter.com/hatewheel/status/731614376935981058\" target=\"_blank\">clarified this a while ago</a>. If you had just asked directly you probably would have got the answer sooner.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T05:27:17-07:00","id":971892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/971242-solar-charm-experiment?p=971891#post971891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay, just to be clear, I don't think it's just members of the Exalted community, John M\u00f8rke (who wrote the Charm) <a href=\"https://twitter.com/hatewheel/status/731614376935981058\" target=\"_blank\">clarified this a while ago</a>. If you had just asked directly you probably would have got the answer sooner.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I have given the player the link to this <i>and </i>Vance's similar answer earlier. They responded with &quot;if they want me to accept it, they can publish an official errata&quot;.<br /> <br /> Believe me, I've exhausted all reasonable avenues of persuading them beforehand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":3443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","user":"aluminiumtrioxid","date":". 09-18-2016, 08:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T06:33:33-07:00","id":971903,"title":"","content":"How about &quot;put your foot down?&quot;<br /> <br /> You're the ST, right? If they want to argue about the rules, you can point them right at the Orichalcum Rule.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, ask them not as their ST, but as their friend. &quot;I don't feel comfortable running it this way.&quot;<br /> <br /> Really, though, not accepting the unanimous answer of the guys <i>who wrote the Charms</i> makes it seem like there's a deeper issue than the text of the Charm. I don't know your players, but this really doesn't sound like a problem we forumites can solve for you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 09-18-2016, 10:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}